    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "\r\n\r\n### **User Journey: Reset/Undo**\r\n\r\n**Scenario:** You are designing a product filter page for an online store. Users can filter by categories, price ranges, and ratings.Your page needs two separate features:\r\n\r\n1. **Reset All:** Goes back to the original product list (no filters).\r\n2. **Undo:** Removes just the *last* change the user made.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n\r\nCreate a user journey diagram that must include the following wireframes:\r\n\r\n1.  **The Original State** when the page first loads.\r\n2.  **At Least Two Filter Changes** (e.g., \"Apply Price Filter,\" then \"Apply Category Filter\").\r\n3.  **A \"Reset\" Path** showing what happens when the user clicks **Reset**.\r\n4.  **An \"Undo\" Path** showing what happens when the user clicks **Undo**.\r\n5.  **Emotional labels** for each step in the path. (e.g., \"Relieved,\" \"Frustrated,\" \"Confident\")."
  },
